  "ruleSetPolicy": "",
  "description": "The Auto Loan Processing System evaluates applicants to determine their eligibility for a car loan. The system ensures responsible lending by assessing financial stability, creditworthiness, and risk factors. It streamlines approvals, reducing manual workload and improving loan processing speed.\n\nThe system evaluates five critical factors:\n\nCredit Score – Determines the applicant’s repayment history and creditworthiness.\nAnnual Income – Ensures the applicant has a stable income to repay the loan.\nEmployment Status – Verifies if the applicant has a secure job or business.\nDebt-to-Income (DTI) Ratio – Measures existing debt load compared to income.\nDown Payment Percentage – Higher down payments reduce lender risk.\n\nThe loan decisions include Approved, Conditional Approval, or Rejected.",
